                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": []
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "e9dea7f3-d6f2-4944-be53-294163db3375",
                        "source_entry_id": "b64a3692-14d2-30a4-9487-9c8bbee1a912",
                        "source_sense_id": "8dbc99d7-7229-3874-a74c-329395c90ca1",
                        "target_lang_word": "romantasy",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "romantasy",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4553973c-b5d2-3d77-8e15-1c1d0ce58bb5",
                                        "entry_id": "d2590d91-18bc-36e2-a63b-3f3292fc80e4",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Romantic fantasy, a subgenre of fantasy literature."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2e0b5d60-9220-4f31-9cfa-ff9f029ccb39",
                                                "sense_id": "4553973c-b5d2-3d77-8e15-1c1d0ce58bb5",
                                                "text": "I want @lara_adrian 's book 7.! -.- sooo bad.! Best romantasy author ever.! (:"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7048b14b-3179-4db8-b4ca-16abeaa64ce7",
                                                "sense_id": "4553973c-b5d2-3d77-8e15-1c1d0ce58bb5",
                                                "text": "Well that's the typical girl in books\nEspecially romance and \"romantasy\""
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "112cbd2b-85bc-49c1-b61f-04e22a3f8f5b",
                                                "sense_id": "4553973c-b5d2-3d77-8e15-1c1d0ce58bb5",
                                                "text": "[Sarah J.] Maas, whose sales jumped 51 per cent this past year and was largely credited by Bloomsbury for a 15 per cent increase in total revenue, is technically classified as sci-fi or “romantasy”."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d705b338-0b42-4c60-b847-4628292748c6",
                                                "sense_id": "4553973c-b5d2-3d77-8e15-1c1d0ce58bb5",
                                                "text": "Morgan Entrekin, chief executive of Grove Atlantic, the publisher behind last year's Booker prize-winner, Paul Lynch's Prophet Song, agrees. “The boom in [romantasy]^([sic]) has been amazing,” he says."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c1324cf4-6455-45b6-9644-04d48c2f7353",
                                                "sense_id": "4553973c-b5d2-3d77-8e15-1c1d0ce58bb5",
                                                "text": "Besides appealing to hordes of existing fans, “Alchemised” has another advantage: It taps into the raging appetite for romantasy, a subgenre that blends fantasy elements like magic, fairies and dragons with love, yearning and explicit sex. In a way, the romantasy explosion — driven by the success of blockbuster authors like Sarah J. Maas and Rebecca Yarros, whose series have sold millions upon millions of copies — stems from the legacy of popular young adult series like “Twilight” and “Harry Potter.”"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4f65b479-a697-3258-80bc-3843438581eb",
                                        "entry_id": "d2590d91-18bc-36e2-a63b-3f3292fc80e4",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A romantic fantasy."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5261d87f-61fe-450a-ae97-8c3b4ed14026",
                                                "sense_id": "4f65b479-a697-3258-80bc-3843438581eb",
                                                "text": "Every hostess knows Blue Willow, the lovers fleeing across the bridge, the turtle doves and all the other romantasies . . ."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "80af406c-a8ee-4b1b-a460-4d05a75f191b",
                                                "sense_id": "4f65b479-a697-3258-80bc-3843438581eb",
                                                "text": "Are we light-hearted? Yes—if we counter warning-weariness by reading Gerald Bullett’s romantasy: When the cat’s away"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c9224524-973e-43fc-9090-a343c021d651",
                                                "sense_id": "4f65b479-a697-3258-80bc-3843438581eb",
                                                "text": "Won’t you be my Valentine “romantasy”."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7fd29abe-d271-402f-a8ea-c62296365c99",
                                                "sense_id": "4f65b479-a697-3258-80bc-3843438581eb",
                                                "text": "The perfect companion to your favorite book series, this coloring book filled with fire-breathing dragons, dagger-wielding warriors, and fierce and lovely fae will make all your romantasies come true."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
